{
  "tema": 7182,
  "slug": "andar-gerundio",
  "titulo": "Andar + gerund = to go around doing something",
  "subtitulo": "Anda diciendo que soy flojo. Ando buscando trabajo.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Andar + gerund = to go around doing, to be (busy) doing, often vaguely or repeatedly: Anda diciendo cosas de ti. Very common in Mexico in everyday speech: ¿Qué andas haciendo? Ando buscando trabajo.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "andar (any tense)",
            "+",
            "gerund"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Like **estar** + gerund, but with a sense of **going around**, repeating, or a vague ongoing activity. **Andar** loses its meaning of _to walk_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Often slightly negative: **anda diciendo**, **anda coqueteando**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**In Mexico** it's everyday and neutral: **¿Qué andas haciendo?** (_What are you up to?_), **ando trabajando**, **anda enfermo** (also **andar** + adjective)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **andar** + gerund = doing it here and there, all over."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Carmen ==anda diciendo== que eres un tonto.",
              "en": "Carmen's going around saying you're an idiot."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==andes esculcando== en mis cajones.",
              "en": "Don't go snooping in my drawers."
            },
            {
              "es": "Esos chavos ==andan coqueteando== con todas.",
              "en": "Those guys go around flirting with every girl."
            },
            {
              "es": "María ==andaba buscando== una falda roja.",
              "en": "María was looking all over for a red skirt."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Qué ==andas haciendo==? —Nada, aquí ==ando==.",
              "en": "—What are you up to? —Nothing, just hanging around."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ando buscando== trabajo.",
              "en": "I'm looking for work."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "comparar",
      "titulo": "Estar or andar?",
      "bloques": [
